  "commits": [
    {
      "sha": "f9594e4036b0ce6b119d8bf3502ee9b7db843ef3",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/f9594e4036b0ce6b119d8bf3502ee9b7db843ef3",
      "message": "Time the import check's rebuild as the steadiest of three runs\n\nA single stall from the host (a collection or a preempted runner) could\nland in the one timed run and fail the bound. Take the run whose longest\nstretch is the smallest share of its total: a stall lands in one run,\nwhile a rebuild that never gives the event loop a turn stretches every\nrun and still fails.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-24T09:34:37Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "5212fc10e0d6ba72827bbcb59bd1cd711d52d9f2",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/5212fc10e0d6ba72827bbcb59bd1cd711d52d9f2",
      "message": "List the HarmonicLabs packages as midgard-node dev dependencies\n\nOnly midgard-node's tests import them; src, scripts and bin do not. The pnpm dependency digest is unchanged.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-24T09:07:06Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "ae2c17bacaf54010739fb13a9d180db893392c50",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/ae2c17bacaf54010739fb13a9d180db893392c50",
      "message": "Say why constant types refuse array and Value tags\n\nThe comments still blamed the HarmonicLabs tag numbering, which the owned constant types no longer use. No term constant holds an array or a Value because the Flat reader reads one as an error term.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-24T09:07:06Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "5585b3d2e6fa859e42e1d5463f58d3cc8ed2139e",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/5585b3d2e6fa859e42e1d5463f58d3cc8ed2139e",
      "message": "Pin every cost twin coefficient by its cost-model parameter name\n\nThe cost twin's only tie to PLUTUS_V3_CANONICAL_COST_MODEL_VIEW went through the HarmonicLabs cost-model reader. The test reads each coefficient by name, in the Plutus V3 parameter order of the pinned aiken, and checks the twin's budgets for tags 0 to 86 over a grid of sizes; every builtin coefficient of those tags must be read.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-24T09:07:06Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "74e91e247a91aad6751ac544a3b3208c0629d33b",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/74e91e247a91aad6751ac544a3b3208c0629d33b",
      "message": "Export the uplc entry of midgard-validation as ESM only\n\nThe CommonJS build of the entry bundles its own copy of the Data classes, so mixing it with other CommonJS entries rejects valid Data. Nothing requires the entry; the plain-ESM fixtures import it.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-24T09:07:06Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "3dc27db7d15c23b0eeea22ddacb3e6523090e0fc",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/3dc27db7d15c23b0eeea22ddacb3e6523090e0fc",
      "message": "Run the transaction differential's reference leg on the script's own bytes\n\nThe reference leg handed the pinned aiken a program it had decoded with Midgard's own Flat and Data decoders and re-encoded, so it no longer read the script independently. Aiken now reads the script's original flat bytes and applies it to the context itself; the context reaches it as a data literal written by a CBOR reader of the leg's own. The builtin-tag check and the step sample take the script's term from the scenario generator instead of decoding the script.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-24T09:07:05Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "2eccd5cc4004b3b781a8254f1d3f3d84a48f10b0",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/2eccd5cc4004b3b781a8254f1d3f3d84a48f10b0",
      "message": "Merge commit 'aca622b661e88b98e1ba160d95587fd740d8b351' into p1/drop-harmonic",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-24T08:45:25Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "250e8649898e1dc09fe3437edf5c7456632fad02",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/250e8649898e1dc09fe3437edf5c7456632fad02",
      "message": "Cost builtins with a TypeScript twin of cek-cost-v1.ak\n\ncomputeMidgardCekBuiltinBudget charges the cost functions and\ncoefficients of the on-chain cost module directly, replacing the\nHarmonicLabs costing and its three corrections (variant E division,\nmultiplyInteger over the product of the sizes, verifyEd25519Signature\nlinear in the message). A differential test holds the twin to the\nreplaced costing over tags 0 to 86 and a grid of sizes. The reference\nevaluator keeps the library's own cost functions for the budget it\ncharges internally, which nothing reads.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-24T08:20:00Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "aca622b661e88b98e1ba160d95587fd740d8b351",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/aca622b661e88b98e1ba160d95587fd740d8b351",
      "message": "Cover our removal builder for a validation-trace conviction of a retired operator\n\nThe validation-trace dispute runner convicts a block whose operator retired\nafter committing it, with descendants committed by that operator and by a\nsecond operator the scheduler rotated to. The shared removal builder prunes\neach descendant under the validation-trace exemption, touching no operator\nnode and paying no reward, then removes the convicted block by slashing the\nretired operator's retired-directory node with the exact fee, reward and\nanchor split.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-24T08:19:29Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "fe1a658e1d14a6a290818c8a7b5b12e8d0bf8f21",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/fe1a658e1d14a6a290818c8a7b5b12e8d0bf8f21",
      "message": "Hold Plutus Data in the owned classes\n\nProduction reads, builds and commits Plutus Data through the owned\nuplc-data classes; the reference evaluator boundary copies Data between\nthem and HarmonicLabs' classes without recursion. Tests and fixtures that\nbuild Data constants now build Midgard's terms, through the new\n@al-ft/midgard-validation/uplc entry for the plain-ESM fixtures.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-24T08:14:18Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "d2a28c01c635a6dd66cc640614bea1c18b047e5a",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/d2a28c01c635a6dd66cc640614bea1c18b047e5a",
      "message": "Read Flat programs into the owned UPLC terms and constants",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-24T07:51:15Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "721d4e980548dc116fb8ec4810e4d8216b5c2f4b",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/721d4e980548dc116fb8ec4810e4d8216b5c2f4b",
      "message": "Write Flat programs with the owned encoder\n\nencodeMidgardCekCardanoFlatProgram now takes any program shaped as the\nencoder reads it and writes it with the owned iterative encoder; the\nHarmonicLabs encoder subclass is gone. Every golden generator --check is\nunchanged.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-24T07:41:18Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "8ea846dab8e4958280ef68e8a56d2d2c81269151",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/8ea846dab8e4958280ef68e8a56d2d2c81269151",
      "message": "Add an owned UPLC value model and Flat encoder to midgard-validation\n\nData classes, constant types numbered as Flat numbers them, term classes\nholding Cardano builtin tags, and an iterative Flat encoder that inverts\nthe Cardano reader. The vendored parts carry the Apache-2.0 attribution\nof the HarmonicLabs packages they derive from. Nothing uses them yet: a\ndifferential test pins the encoder byte-identical to the encoder\nproduction uses today over every fixture, corpus and vector-table program.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-24T07:36:53Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "23cebbdce3a0e61ec8f09c43e5e8e77f3563d1ff",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/23cebbdce3a0e61ec8f09c43e5e8e77f3563d1ff",
      "message": "Drop the HarmonicLabs packages nothing imports\n\nmidgard-node-tools declared all six HarmonicLabs packages, midgard-fault-proofs\ndeclared cbor and midgard-node declared bytestring and pair; none of them is\nimported. The six midgard-validation barrels imported plutus-data, uplc and\nplutus-machine for side effects only. The lockfile and the flake pnpm\ndependency hash follow.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-24T07:22:39Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "796c39fc51226b1512c75bd808d8794e0166be8d",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/796c39fc51226b1512c75bd808d8794e0166be8d",
      "message": "Remove the removal-builder overrides the validation-trace tests no longer use",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-24T01:16:21Z"
    }
